WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.430
Superhero movies have been the biggest thing
at the box office for the past ten years,

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.400
and they don't show any sign of slowing down
in 2019.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.400
Here's everything you need to know about the
upcoming comic-inspired blockbusters that

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.690
are set to blow you away!

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:19.450
With a runtime of just 75 minutes, 2007’s
animated Superman: Doomsday film barely resembled

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:23.920
the groundbreaking 1994 Death of Superman
comic book saga it was based on.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:29.400
Fortunately, it taught Warner Bros. a lesson:
fans want the whole story of Superman’s

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.420
climactic, bone-shattering battle against
the monstrous Doomsday, and now we’re going

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:33.920
to get it.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:39.700
That began with the all-new animated Death
of Superman, which debuted at Comic-Con International

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:44.969
in 2018, and expanded the story to feature
the full Justice League taking on Doomsday

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:46.080
before Superman arrived.

00:00:46.789 --> 00:00:51.100
It went down so well with critics that its
follow-up, Reign of the Supermen, is getting

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.560
a full-on theatrical release as a two-day
double-feature event.

00:00:55.449 --> 00:00:59.760
Like its comic book counterpart, Reign of
the Supermen features four pretenders to Superman's

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:06.100
recently vacated throne, the Cyborg Superman,
The Eradicator, Steel, and Superboy, a teenage

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.830
clone described as "Superman if he'd been
raised by the Kardashians."

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.740
Get ready, it’s set to hit theaters on January
29th, 2019.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.811
If there was any doubt that the upcoming Captain
Marvel film would be set in the ‘90s with

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:23.200
plenty of tributes to the favorite cinematic
hits of that decade, it was taken care of

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.840
when the first trailer was released.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.909
There’s a scene where star Brie Larson crashes
through the roof of a Blockbuster Video, right

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:33.760
into the Action section, and it doesn’t
get much more ‘90s than that.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:39.979
In the comics, Carol Danvers has a long history
that dates back to 1968, and she's gone by

00:01:39.979 --> 00:01:45.700
several heroic codenames, including Ms. Marvel,
Binary, and Warbird, and even had her powers

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:48.140
permanently stolen by Rogue from the X-Men.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:53.580
Since 2012, she’s taken on the identity
of Captain Marvel and become a fan favorite,

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.860
and now she’s poised to star in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe’s first film focused

00:01:57.860 --> 00:01:59.260
on a female superhero.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.440
That doesn’t mean she’ll be alone, though.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:06.200
Since it’s a flashback story, moviegoers
can expect to see the return of a few familiar

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.900
faces, including Korath the Pursuer and Ronan
the Accuser, last seen in Guardians of the

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:15.630
Galaxy, and a younger Nick Fury and Agent
Coulson in the earlier days of SHIELD.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.620
"What is this?"

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:17.630
"It's a SHIELD logo."

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:21.280
"Does announcing your identity on clothing
help with the covert part of your job?"

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.040
Throw in the fact that Carol was positioned
as Nick Fury’s secret weapon at the end

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:29.080
of Infinity War, and we know exactly where
we want to be when Captain Marvel hits the

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.220
screen on March 8th.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:35.820
The word "reshoots" became a dirty one among
DC fans after the disasters that were Suicide

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:40.750
Squad and Justice League, but that hasn't
stopped Warner Bros. from recalling the Shazam!

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:42.740
cast for some last minute tweaks.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.300
This time, though, director David F. Sandberg
has insisted that the tone of the movie, which

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:51.370
star Zachary Levi described as “Big meets
Superman,” won’t be altered.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.960
That’s good news for DC fans who are desperate
for something lighter.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.180
Judging by the trailer, Shazam appears to
be following more in the footsteps of the

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:04.160
colorful adventure of Aquaman rather than
the grim darkness of Batman v. Superman.

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:09.680
There are plenty of jokes, lots of action,
and best of all, Levi actually acts like an

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.400
enthusiastic, excited kid in the body of a
superhero.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.300
"That's crazy, right?"

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.080
"What are your superpowers?"

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:16.560
"Superpowers?

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.320
Dude, I don’t even know how to pee in this
thing!"

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:23.660
After debuting in 1940 as the original Captain
Marvel, Shazam quickly grew to be even more

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:28.000
popular than Superman, and hopefully, this
movie will show a whole new generation of

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.540
fans why when it hits theaters on April 5th.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:35.580
It’s the ultimate wish-fulfillment fantasy
of kids who want to be superheroes themselves,

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.240
with a ton of magical action thrown in for
good measure.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:43.420
Traditionally, three DC Universe Animated
Original Movies are released every year.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:49.520
It's been this way since 2009 when Wonder
Woman, Green Lantern: First Flight and Superman/Batman:

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.880
Public Enemies came out.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:56.620
For 2019, though, the studio confirmed that
it plans to drop a total of four films, including

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:00.840
one based on Jeph Loeb and Jim Lee's acclaimed
Batman storyline: Hush.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:06.220
Originally released as a 12-part, year-long
epic, Hush gave readers a mystery story with

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:11.110
a seemingly simple solution, but with enough
complications to bring in Batman’s entire

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.040
gallery of foes.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:16.660
With memorable moments like Batman having
to take down Superman after the Man of Steel

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:21.350
was possessed by Poison Ivy, the Dark Knight’s
relationship with Catwoman being taken to

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:25.870
the next level, and the introduction of the
sinister madman called Hush, it’s been a

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.580
fan favorite since it was released.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:33.900
Avengers: Endgame is coming out on April 26th,
almost a year to the day after Infinity War

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:34.400
was hit theaters.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:39.460
After the brutal downer of an ending that
saw Thanos committing galactic genocide and

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:43.380
killing off half of the MCU’s superheroes,
though, it feels like we’ve been waiting

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:46.690
a lot longer than a single year to find out
what happens next.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:51.240
In fact, we didn’t even know the name of
the movie until the teaser finally came out,

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:55.220
but giving it the title “Endgame” is far
from the only ominous thing we’ve gotten

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:56.000
from the trailer.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:01.400
We’ve seen a world where Tony Stark is recording
his final message to Pepper Potts, perhaps

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:05.730
paving the way for her to take on her own
suit of armor as Rescue, where Hawkeye has

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:10.280
gone rogue and changed his identity to Ronin,
and where it looks like the only way the heroes

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.960
can stop Thanos is with the help of… Ant-Man?

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.040
"Ant-Man?

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:15.000
Ant-Man!

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.200
I know, I know you know that!"

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:20.120
When this guy is your only hope, you know
things have gone seriously bad.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:26.060
With the Fox-Disney merger now cleared, Marvel's
merry mutants are destined for the MCU.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:32.120
As a result, X-Men: Dark Phoenix will be a
swan song for Fox's hit-and-miss X-Men franchise.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.800
It hasn’t been an easy road to get here,
though.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:39.360
The initial release date was bumped to buy
time for extensive reshoots, and there were

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.840
rumors that Disney might just can the movie
entirely.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:46.520
When it comes out on June 7th, it’ll be
the second time that the X-Movies have tried

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:50.830
to adapt the legendary Dark Phoenix Saga,
and fans alre already worried that it’s

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.440
going to be botched all over again.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:57.640
Only time will tell if Sophie Turner will
fare better than Famke Janssen as the doomed

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:02.560
Jean Grey, but if this really is the end of
Fox’s X-Men, then anything could happen.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.960
Oh, come on, you didn’t really think Spider-Man
was dead after Infinity War, did you?

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:11.900
Whatever happens in Endgame, Tom Holland will
be back in action as Peter Parker on July

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:15.740
5th, and while he’s not quite fading to
dust on the moons of Jupiter, he’s still

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.380
going to be pretty far from home.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:22.020
With Peter and his classmates embarking on
a trip to Europe, it seems Spider-Man will

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:26.600
be taking on Mysterio, and maybe even Hydro
Man, in places like Venice and London.

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:32.120
Mysterio, a movie special effects genius turned
super-criminal con man, is an interesting

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:33.120
choice for a villain.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.080
"Who is that guy?"

00:06:35.092 --> 00:06:37.100
"He's like Iron Man and Thor rolled into one."

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.110
"He’s no Spider-Man."

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:42.370
Like the Vulture, who took center stage in
Homecoming, he’s one of Spider-Man’s classic

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:47.840
Sinister Six, and the hints that he’ll be
discrediting Spidey by acting as a rival superhero

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.980
rather than a villain could lead to some really
great fun.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:55.139
Don’t expect Jake Gyllenhaal to hide his
handsome looks under Mysterio’s classic

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.440
comic book bubble helmet for too long, though.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:02.260
The New Mutants was sold on the idea that
it would be a twist on the familiar tropes

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:07.180
that we’ve seen in superhero films: it’s
a horror movie that just happens to star characters

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:08.460
from Marvel Comics.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:12.880
Director Josh Boone seemed like the perfect
fit, and his passion for the project made

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:14.400
Fox want to take a chance on him.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:19.400
Unfortunately, according to reports, the studio
wasn't impressed with what he turned in.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:25.419
Instead of its scheduled release in April
of 2018, The New Mutants was pushed back ten

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.880
whole months to February 2019.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.699
The official reason, according to The Hollywood
Reporter, was that the studio wanted to avoid

00:07:32.699 --> 00:07:38.110
overlap with Deadpool 2 in certain overseas
territories, but then it was pushed back even

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:42.270
further to August, fueling rumors that there
was something other than a simple scheduling

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:43.220
conflict going on.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:47.920
Considering that the source material contains
some of the most legendarily scary stories

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:52.000
to ever be featured on the comics page, we’re
hoping they manage to nail it.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:57.400
At first glance, the Fatal Five seem like
a pretty unusual set of villains for an animated

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:58.620
Justice League story.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:03.970
Created by teenage writer Jim Shooter in the
‘60s, the quintet of bad guys were originally

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:08.660
villains for the Legion of Super-Heroes, a
team based in the distant future of the 30th

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:09.160
Century.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:13.780
Knowing all of that, it won’t surprise you
that they’re a weird bunch of characters,

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:18.720
including the Emerald Empress, who gains her
power from a giant floating magical eyeball,

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:22.020
and Validus, who shoots lightning bolts out
of his exposed brain.

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:26.820
On August 6th, it seems that they’ll be
taking the fight to our very own 21st century

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:31.520
Justice League, which might be a stealthy
way of introducing the Legion of Super-Heroes

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:34.800
to the ongoing line of DC Universe Original
Movies.

00:08:35.069 --> 00:08:38.700
While they haven’t been regularly seen in
comics for a few years, they’ve built up

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:41.420
a dedicated fan-base over the past 60 years.

00:08:42.029 --> 00:08:46.280
Of course, this could just be a story of the
Justice League taking on a bunch of ultra-powerful

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:50.080
baddies that even most comic book fans haven’t
seen them tangle with before.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:54.009
That alone makes this one worth checking out,
especially since it’s going to be available

00:08:54.009 --> 00:08:57.760
on DC’s streaming service the same day it’s
released to the rest of the world.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:03.240
He's arguably the most iconic villain in comic
book history, but the Joker has never been

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:07.140
given a truly definitive backstory in print
or on the big screen.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:11.759
For many fans, that’s even part of his timeless
appeal, but for those of us with a little

00:09:11.759 --> 00:09:16.769
more curiosity, Warner Bros. will be offering
up a story of the Clown Prince of Crime’s

00:09:16.769 --> 00:09:19.160
earliest days on October 4th, 2019.

00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:23.840
With the help of director Todd Phillips and
three-time Academy Award-nominated actor Joaquin

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:28.639
Phoenix, Joker will tell the story of the
man who ultimately becomes Batman’s deadliest

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:29.780
arch-nemesis.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:34.700
The film is rumored to be a mixture of Alan
Moore and Brian Bolland’s classic Batman:

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:39.579
The Killing Joke graphic novel and Martin
Scorsese's classic King of Comedy, and was

00:09:39.579 --> 00:09:45.510
confirmed by the Warner Bros. 2019 Editorial
guide as, quote, "an exploration of Arthur

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:50.610
Fleck, a man disregarded by society, [and]
is not only a gritty character study, but

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.459
also a broader cautionary tale."

00:09:53.459 --> 00:09:58.829
We know that this will be the fourth DC Universe
Animated Original Movie released in 2019,

00:09:58.829 --> 00:10:02.360
but Wonder Woman: Bloodlines still remains
something of a mystery.

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:06.780
Since there’s no existing Wonder Woman comic
with that title, Bloodlines is set to be an

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:11.259
original story, but all we have to go on so
far is an "ominous" teaser poster for the

00:10:11.259 --> 00:10:16.490
October 22nd release, featuring a crumbling
temple, possibly hinting at the destruction

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:17.560
of Themyscira.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:21.910
The success of the live-action Wonder Woman
movie meant that bringing Diana Prince back

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:24.680
to the animated DC universe was a no-brainer.

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:30.360
The Amazon last appeared in a DC Universe
animated film back in 2009, and while it was

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:33.760
critically acclaimed, it didn’t exactly
fly off the shelves.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:39.880
In fact, as longtime DC animator Bruce Timm
revealed back in 2018, the slow sales actually

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:44.460
made Warner Bros. can a planned Batgirl movie
based on the Batgirl: Year One comic.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:47.560
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.880
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:54.500
Subscribe to our YouTube channel, and hit
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

